A MK Studio "starpack" is a Tcl runtime (a "tclkit") with MK Studio's own files appended. Components of that runtime:

  Tcl and Tk            Tcl/Tk license (BSD-style).     https://www.tcl-lang.org/software/tcltk/license.html
                        Included: Tcl and Tk 8.6.18 (Linux, Windows, macOS); Tcl 8.5.17 and the 2014 Tcl 8.6.3 are used only in tests.
  Metakit and Mk4tcl    MIT-style license.              https://github.com/jcw/metakit  (Jean-Claude Wippler)
                        The database engine and its Tcl binding. The runtimes contain the author's fork with 64-bit file positions,
                        https://github.com/atyr647/metakit (a copy of the source at the commit named in tools/vendor/METAKIT-FORK is
                        kept in tools/vendor/; the license text, license.terms, is part of it and unchanged: Copyright (c) 1996-2007
                        Jean-Claude Wippler).
  tclvfs, itcl, tcllib-style helpers
                        the same Tcl/BSD-style licenses as Tcl itself (as built into the tclkit).
  zlib                  zlib license.                   https://zlib.net/zlib_license.html
                        1.3.1 in the runtimes built in CI (the 2014 test-only tclkits carry 1.2.8)
  tclkit runtime        built by the KitCreator project (Roy Keene) - https://kitcreator.rkeene.org/ . All three
                        runtimes are compiled in CI from KitCreator (a pinned revision, kept in tools/vendor/ - MIT, with a few Tcl-licensed files,
                        see the LICENSE inside it; tools/build-kit.sh and the
                        build workflow): Linux in a glibc 2.28 container, Windows with mingw-w64, macOS natively on
                        each Mac. The old prebuilt kits from https://tclkits.rkeene.org/ (tools/fetch-runtimes.sh checks
                        their SHA-1) are only used by tests.

mksync                MK Studio's own flush library (native/mksync/mksync.c, MIT, see LICENSE). It is compiled together with Tcl's
                        stub-library initialiser, generic/tclStubLib.c from the Tcl 8.6.18 source archive that the build checks
                        against a pinned SHA-256 (Tcl/Tk license, as above); nothing else of Tcl is linked in.

mkit-sql              the standard-SQL engine in mkstudio.vfs/lib/mkitsql (a vendored copy; SOURCE names the commit),
                        https://github.com/atyr647/mkit-sql - written for this project by the same author. It is
                        distributed here as part of MK Studio under this repository's MIT license (LICENSE). The mkit-sql
                        repository carries the same MIT text (LICENSE) since 0.4.1.

The Windows installer is built with NSIS (zlib/libpng-style license, https://nsis.sourceforge.io/), which only runs at
build time; its stub is part of the installer.

The installer and the icons are made for MK Studio (tools/make-icons.py) and are covered by LICENSE.

Where a runtime ships its own license files they are inside the starpack (Tcl's "license.terms" in the library
directory). If any attribution here is missing or wrong, please open an issue.
